  "goodToKnow": "Die Einschaltquote (often just die Quote) is the viewing figures or ratings of a TV programme, measured by the AGF using panel households. The Sunday crime series Tatort regularly draws high ratings. The most-watched broadcast in German TV history was the 2014 World Cup final, with about 34.6 million viewers. Critics complain about Quotendruck (pressure for ratings). Plural: die Einschaltquoten."
